`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
**Key diagnosis from renders:**
1. White belly hulls (color 8) are too small and sit too close to Z=200 center — they're hidden behind the black back hulls in every view
2. Beak cones are tiny and don't protrude far enough forward (low Z) to be visible from top
3. Flippers are too close to body center (X=176/224) — need 10-15 units wider
4. The front view is almost entirely dark because white elements don't extend far enough in Z
**Fix strategy:** Push white hulls aggressively forward (Z 165-175), enlarge them, extend beak to Z=140, widen flippers
